  "text": "\r\n\t\t Election Information | Hudson, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     Departments   \t\t\t \n     Boards and Committees   \t\t\t \n     Our Community   \t\t\t \n     How Do I   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t November 3, 2026 State General Election Sample Ballot \r\n\t\t\t Absentee Voting Information \r\n\t\t\t Citizen's Petition Warrant Articles \r\n\t\t\t Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2026 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2025 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2024 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2023 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2022 Election/Results Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2021 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2020 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2019 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2018 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2017 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2016 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2015 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2014 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2013 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2012 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2011 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2010 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2009 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2008 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2007 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t\t 2006 Election Results/Ballots \r\n\t\t\t NH Voter Information Look-up \r\n\t\t\t Polling Locations \r\n\t\t\t Registering to Vote \r\n\t\t\t Voter Traffic Patterns \r\nHome \nDepartments \nTown Clerk \nElection Information \r\nElection Information\t\t \r\nVoter Registrations \nAny Hudson resident, who is at least 18 years old, may register to vote in person at the Town Clerk's Office during regular office hours, 8 am-4:30 pm. Monday through Friday. You must bring a photo ID and proof of residency and citizenship. The new New Hampshire State requirements  are available here. \nPlease see  Registering to Vote   for more detailed information. \nChange in Party Affiliation \nRegistered voters may change their party affiliation with the town clerk, or, at any scheduled meeting of the supervisors of the checklist except for during the period of time between the first day of the filing period for the primary election and/or the presidential primary election and the date of the primary election itself. You must appear in person at the Town Clerk's Office during regular office hours to request a change in party affiliation and will be asked to provide identification. Any person may change party registration at any primary, upon oath or affirmation to the same effect, but he shall not be permitted to vote the ballot of any party at such primary ( RSA 654:34(b) ). \nAbsentee Ballot Applications \nCollege students who are registered to vote in Hudson Town/School elections may request an absentee ballot; complete and mail it to the Town Clerk's Office, 12 School Street, Hudson, NH 03051 or fax it to 603-816-1292. \n**A copy of your New Hampshire Driver's License must accompany your application, per  RSA 659:13, II(a),   or, the application must be notarized. Please note: Notarized forms cannot be faxed. \nRegistered voters who will be away during State or Town Elections may request an absentee ballot by completing either, the Application for Town Election Absentee Ballot   form and mailing it to the Town Clerk's Office, 12 School Street, Hudson, NH 03051, or, by faxing it to 603-816-1292. \n**A copy of your New Hampshire Driver's License must accompany your application, per  RSA 659:13, II(a) ,   or, the application must be notarized. Please note: Notarized forms cannot be faxed. \nPlease see  Absentee Ballot Information  for more detailed information. \nQuestions? Contact Town Clerk, Emilie Leclerc at (603) 886-6003. \r\n         Election Dates & Deadlines \n         Voter Information Look Up \n         Polling Locations \n         Absentee Voting \n         Election Results \n     